WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:04.560
That way.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.270
You never cease to amaze me, Reina.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.400
I can't believe you can sense a 
Chaos Teller inside the Fog of Silence.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.950
Well, whenever we enter a Story Zone,
 she also immediately gets lost.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.970
What do you mean "immediately," Tao?

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.910
I still can't believe it, though...

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:25.180
That there are so many worlds 
within the Fog of Silence.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.290
They're not "worlds." They're Story Zones.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.220
You're right, Shane.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.420
And inside each Story Zone, the same 
story is played out again and again.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.510
You're finally wrapping your head 
around all this, kid.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.680
Of course, we could hardly 
believe it ourselves at first.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.680
The only people who can travel 
through the Fog of Silence

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.390
are those who have been given 
a blank Book of Fate.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.440
Most don't even know it exists,
 so that's only natural.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.740
Let's head to the next Story Zone.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.120
We came out of the fog 
only to find more fog?

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.170
No, Ex... The Fog of Silence
 is creeping into this Story Zone.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.710
That's a sign the Story Zone's
 about to collapse.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.880
Collapse?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.870
The welcoming committee's here.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.750
Already?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.930
These villains were created from nothing.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.210
You there, young people with bright futures!

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.560
Leave this to Don Quixote,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.150
the proud knight of La Mancha!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:30.760
Don...

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.020
Quixote?

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.410
Don Quixote's Faith

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.080
That was harder than I thought it would be.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.540
But...

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.790
What's with the old guy?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.290
He shows up out of nowhere, 
then just drops to the ground...

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.760
My back! My back!

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.310
The devil's strike hit me!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.180
Well done, though!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.310
You even did those peculiar transformations...

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.810
Ow, ow, ow...

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.770
Are you okay?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.520
Sancho?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.190
Is that you, Sancho?!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.190
No, my name is Ex...

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.040
What?!

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.690
Sancho, it's me, your master! 
Don Quixote! Don't you remember?!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.990
My back is killing me...

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.530
Come! Let's go, Sancho!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.740
Go where?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.300
Where else?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.450
The devil's servants will 
make their move on the town next.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.710
We must go and save the innocent townsfolk!

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.680
Rocinante! Where are you, Rocinante?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.460
Rocinante?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.550
If you mean the donkey
 you were riding...

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.840
What?!

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.590
Ow, ow, ow...

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.130
My back's acting up again!
Yeow, ow, ouch...

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.930
So be it...

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.890
Pain, pain, go away!

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.440
That feels so nice!

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.400
Come on, Sancho! Hurry it up!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.050
My name is Ex, though...

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.950
Is it a good idea to follow this geezer?

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.490
We don't yet know anything 
about the Chaos Teller.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.290
We should check out the town first.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.170
There she is!

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.230
The fog hasn't come this far yet, huh?

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.650
It may only be a matter of time.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.510
Hey, it's the lying old man!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.350
The lying old man's back!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.430
Lying old man?

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.810
Most of the people here 
haven't seen the devil's servants.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.810
Well, no time to stand around and chat!

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.480
I need to go patrol the city.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.070
Sancho, take these folks to the church.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:09.350
Dulcinea will provide 
them food if you ask her.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.950
Dulcinea?

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:17.070
Don Quixote's the same as ever, I see.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.340
Are you...

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.130
Yes, I'm Dulcinea.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.050
Who are they?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.810
Refugees from the towns to the east
who fled for their lives.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.870
Um...

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:39.560
Dulcinea, you seem to know 
a lot about Don Quixote.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.770
True...

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:47.680
Once upon a time, there lived an 
old man in the land of La Mancha.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.670
Day in and day out, he did nothing
 but read chivalric tales.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.310
Eventually he began to believe 
he himself was a knight.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.210
He donned armor and helmet,

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.620
and took off on a quest to go 
right the wrongs of the world.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.310
His name was Alonso Quixano.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:10.800
And as a knight, he called himself 
Don Quixote of La Mancha.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.060
That's all I know.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.600
Dulcinea!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.730
We can draw water ourselves...

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:22.610
No, this is a task that heaven has given me.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.160
We're serving food over there,
 if you'd like some...

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.950
So that knight is the main 
character of this Story Zone?

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.790
But if the story's proceeding like it's 
supposed to, why are there so many villains?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.120
It's just one mystery after another...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.420
Don't tell me that old Don Quixote is...

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.420
It's too soon to jump to conclusions.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.420
Let's just start by gathering information.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.380
All righty, we'll split up and 
see what we can find out.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.670
Let's meet up here in an hour.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.980
Did you hear? The eastern towns
 have been wiped out.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.550
You're telling me old Don Quixote 
wasn't lying after all?

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.780
Hey, you kids.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:08.280
Huh? Aren't you the girl 
who was with the lying old man?

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.740
Can you tell me more
 about the lying old man?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.320
What do you think?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.180
I don't particularly mind...

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.870
But you can't have any of our snacks.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.470
O-Of course not...

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.210
Hurry it up!

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.380
We might die if we stay here!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.880
Good grief...

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:35.430
My Book of Fate says I'm supposed to die 
peacefully, surrounded by grandkids...

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.760
And mine says I'm supposed 
to divorce my loser husband

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.560
and marry a younger man!

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.440
What do you think of that?!

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.800
What?!

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.440
Wow...

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.270
Should we evacuate too?

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.280
That rumor's gotta be bogus.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.080
Oh, Sancho!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:07:59.910
Don Quixote!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.580
Worry not.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.980
The devil's servants are 
nowhere to be found for now.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:06.840
Um...

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:07.460
What is it?

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:10.590
The townspeople are calling
 you a liar... Why is that?

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.670
It doesn't matter what other people say.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.930
I'm doing what I believe in!

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.790
And someday everyone will realize—

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.670
That doesn't matter!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.390
A knight's job is to bring peace 
and victory to the people.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.330
Isn't that right, Sancho?

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:28.940
But I...

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:33.020
If you have time to ask 
dumb questions, go patrol!

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.570
If but a single servant of the devil 
makes it inside these walls,

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.710
we'll have big trouble!

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.830
I'm off to check the southern gate!

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:45.610
<i>I never had...</i>

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:52.130
Have some warm soup, everyone.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.880
Thank you, Holy Maiden...

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.350
How'd it go?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.470
I didn't really learn anything.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.640
Would you like some more?

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:03.930
Please!

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.080
Dulcinea's really popular.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.330
She came to this town right about the time 
the rumors of strange monsters started.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:17.160
She volunteered to treat people's wounds...

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.700
Everybody calls her the Holy Maiden now.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.120
Holy Maiden?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.510
Monsters are coming from the east!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:26.670
We need to get out of here!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.620
We can't!

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.080
These people are too injured to move!

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:31.840
Should we run and leave them behind?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.420
We don't have a choice, I guess.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.840
Fear not!

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.680
Anyone who can take up arms,

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.590
stand with me and defend the town!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.930
Don Quixote is right!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.730
Many of you thought him a liar,

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.360
but now the devil's servants are upon us.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.070
Please, believe in him now 
and take up your swords!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.580
The Story Zone's starting to collapse!

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.150
Oh, no...

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.710
It's all over now.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.340
Nay, this is not the end!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.840
The proud knight of La Mancha, 
the knight of the lion...

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.720
Don Quixote is here!

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:23.970
Let us show these accursed servants 
of the devil what we have faith in!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.350
He's right!

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.560
I-I'll fight, too!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.480
Me, too!

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.110
Even the wounded are volunteering to fight.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.190
Are you just going to sit back and watch?

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.320
W-We get it!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.440
We'll gather the other soldiers.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.870
All right! We'll buy time while you do!

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:45.240
Sancho, to my side!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.370
No, my name isn't...

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.460
Sancho, we're leaving.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.540
Right...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.920
Let's protect the faith of Don Quixote!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:31.330
Don Quixote!

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.870
He's a hero, huh?

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.070
Don Quixote really fought hard,
 don't you think?

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.290
He took a break because of his back
halfway through the fight, though.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.090
Wow, what a meal!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.670
Huh? Where's Reina?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.550
Still eating.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.340
Still?

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.550
Well, whatever.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:43.760
They gave us a place to stay, 
so let's hit the hay.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.100
I'm going to go take a look around the city.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.350
Yell if something happens, kid.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.030
No taking action on your own.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.160
I know.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:58.000
I'm doing what I believe in!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.950
What brings you out at 
this late hour, Sancho?

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.740
You were quite the hero today.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.500
The real hero was Don Quixote!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:15.670
No, the old man simply played out his role

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.130
in accordance with his Book of Fate.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:19.990
<i>I-I know that voice...</i>

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.760
The knight of La Mancha, 
the man everyone admires...

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.720
What a splendid role to play.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:30.350
But he's really just a sad little puppet

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.310
dancing to the Storyteller's tune.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.280
No!

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.400
Don Quixote is living his life
 chasing what he believes in!

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.400
He's not a puppet!

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.860
It's quite possible that even as we speak,

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.610
Red Riding Hood is trembling
 inside the wolf's stomach.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:45.990
Where are you?!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:49.180
We are always right beside you.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.200
You're...

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.080
I bid you goodnight.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.350
Wait!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.430
Ex?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.210
Why were you shouting?

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.430
Well...

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.640
Dulcinea?

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.430
I just told Reina,

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:12.770
but you should know that 
I am not a real person.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:17.900
I was created by Don Quixote's fantasies.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:18.560
But...

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.480
You look real to me.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:26.530
His imagination is so strong it 
has the power to warp reality.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.910
Is that possible?

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:32.290
It all began when he mistook the 
windmill on the hill for a monster

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.450
and challenged it to battle.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.120
That's when the devil's 
servants began appearing,

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.210
and when I was created.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.380
Then those villains...

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:46.300
It's likely that his strong desire to 
be a hero created the Chaos Teller

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.970
and gave rise to the villains.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:49.890
That's terrible...

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:55.020
I heard Don Quixote say he'd be going
 to the place it all began tomorrow...

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.540
The windmill on the hill.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.310
I'm worried.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.610
When the secret of the windmill is revealed,

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:07.780
will Don Quixote be blamed 
for causing all of this?

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.200
There's no need to worry!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.740
How much of that did you hear?

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.120
Even if everyone blames me,

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.920
I cannot betray my beliefs!

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:23.500
Worry not, my beautiful princess.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.760
Don Quixote...

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:26.970
Sancho!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:27.880
Y-Yes?!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.260
You did well today.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.640
I hope to see more of it tomorrow.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:39.310
The Chaos Teller might be 
hiding in the windmill.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.020
Make sure you're ready.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:41.940
But...

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.110
What's wrong?

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:46.030
He finally became a real hero,

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:50.110
and Don Quixote is trying to 
put an end to that himself.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.530
Is this really...

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:57.090
If we don't fix this, the Story Zone
 will just outright collapse.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:00.620
Don't overthink it.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:05.040
More villains?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:08.170
What's going on?

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.380
A huge monster!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.510
You should run, too!

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.140
Huge, huh?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.100
How big are we talking, I wonder?

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.020
Let's hurry!

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:30.570
Well, they weren't kidding.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:35.830
The Chaos Teller attached itself to the windmill of
 Don Quixote's fantasies to manifest!

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.220
Seriously?

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.790
I guess anything goes here...

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.000
The wall is destroyed!

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.550
Everybody's going to die!

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:47.800
Stay strong!

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:51.090
It saved us the effort of going to find it.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.200
I, Don Quixote, will hold it off!

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:56.930
Go with the others! 
They've already evacuated!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:57.890
B-But...

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.830
What is that?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.640
A windmill giant?

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.200
Are you okay?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.030
Get the children out of here!

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:15.910
Got it!

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.240
Thanks, old man!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.500
Here it comes.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:31.460
I'd love to find out how that thing works.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.090
The windmill!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.300
Everyone, take cover!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:40.360
Making tornadoes, are you?

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.640
It's the same as last time, giant!

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:46.850
Today, I defeat you 
and stay true to my beliefs!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.820
Hey, you'll get blown away!

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.190
He's crazy.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:54.150
This is nothing more than a spring breeze!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.070
You can do it, old man Don Quixote!

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.620
My faith will not break!

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.580
He's holding on...

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:09.630
We should back him up!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.180
Hang in there!

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:31.100
How pathetic...

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:32.200
Please!

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.390
Stop that monster!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:37.990
Be the knight I couldn't be,

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.780
and save the people of this town...

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:44.350
Ex!

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.240
That's not fair...

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:50.080
Calling me by my name 
at the very last minute.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:55.340
I will protect your faith!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.650
All right!

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.280
Let's get excited and do this.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.150
Cinderella!

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:00.970
Goliath!

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:01.850
Robin Hood!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:02.350
Alice!

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:03.850
Connect!

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:18.420
Is it time for another 
adventure in Wonderland?

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.000
What?

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:28.300
Fine, then!

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:35.000
What terrible manners!

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.010
Ex!

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.380
Unbreakable Glass Slippers!

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:48.730
Myth of Savage Valor!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.650
Sherwood Gale!

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:57.550
We can't even get close?

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.950
Leave it to me!

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.700
Ex?

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.410
Let me your power, Red Riding Hood!

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.510
It's me, Red Riding Hood!

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:23.890
Liars get punished!

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.720
Beware the Wolf!

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:47.990
Well done.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.390
Don Quixote! Everyone!

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:53.880
Dulcinea!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.750
You've finally put an end 
to the nightmare, haven't you?

00:19:56.980 --> 00:20:00.030
I'm just like that windmill giant...

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.880
I don't belong in this world.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.230
Dulcinea...

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.470
There's no time.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.930
I'm going to return this world
 to its proper state.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:12.020
When I do, you will probably disappear.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.020
Along with everyone's memories of you.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:15.150
Very well.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.440
I do not mind.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.110
Dulcinea!

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:23.530
I promise that I alone will never forget you.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:25.990
Thank you.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.690
What a cool dude.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.250
Pretentious old man...

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.290
Don Quixote, I'm grateful to you, too.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.540
Thank you so much!

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.290
Till we meet again, Ex.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:40.920
Indeed!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.230
All right, here I go.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.920
Teller of tales, 
drowned in a maelstrom of chaos...

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:57.190
By my words, I now begin the tuning...

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:19.340
What happened to the windmill giant?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:23.670
Having another dream again, master?

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.260
Sancho... Is that you, Sancho?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.050
You look different...

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.130
What? I've had this face since I was born.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.950
Enough of your silliness.

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:36.020
Come now. We're leaving.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.140
Right!

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:39.770
Watch over me, Dulcinea!

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:43.030
Are you talking to your
 fantasy princess again?

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.400
She's no fantasy!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:48.700
Dulcinea's smile is always within my heart!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.650
Let's go, Sancho!

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.640
First, to the village of El Toboso!

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.540
That's the real Sancho?

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.210
He doesn't look a thing like Ex...

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:05.130
But maybe they've got similar vibes?

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:08.010
Seems like he's got pretty keen 
intuition at least, that old man.

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:12.100
Guys... that doesn't help at all.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.030
What a relief.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:15.130
Yeah.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:17.230
This Story Zone's back to normal.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:20.730
Is something wrong?

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:23.530
Actually, I ran into him last night.

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:24.570
Him?

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.030
That man named Loki...

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:28.450
He's...

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:32.330
<i>Yes, in my homeland where I first met Reina...</i>

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:34.830
<i>He did the same thing.</i>
